#. type: SS
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable fedora-41 fedora-rawhide
#: mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0 opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "I<COMMAND>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable fedora-41 fedora-rawhide
#: mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0 opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Specifies the action to perform on the object.  The set of possible actions "
"depends on the object type.  As a rule, it is possible to B<add>,B< delete> "
"and B<show> (or B<list> ) objects, but some objects do not allow all of "
"these operations or have some additional commands. The B<help> command is "
"available for all objects. It prints out a list of available commands and "
"argument syntax conventions."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable fedora-41 fedora-rawhide
#: mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0 opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"If no command is given, some default command is assumed.  Usually it is "
"B<list> or, if the objects of this class cannot be listed, B<help>."
msgstr ""

